### render_link (lines 363-401)
```rust
fn render_link(&mut self, svg: &mut SvgElem, state: &State, dest: &Destination, size: Size) {
    let mut a = svg.elem("a");
    if !state.transform.is_identity() {
        a.attr("transform", SvgTransform(state.transform));
    }

    match dest {
        Destination::Url(url) => {
            a.attr("href", url.as_str());
            a.attr("xlink:href", url.as_str());
        }
        Destination::Position(_) => {
            // TODO: Links on the same page could be supported.
        }
        Destination::Location(loc) => {
            if let Some(resolver) = self.link_resolver
                && let Some(link) = resolver.resolve(*loc)
                && let Ok(uri) = link.into_relative_uri()
            {
                a.attr("href", &uri);
                a.attr("xlink:href", &uri);
            }
        }
    }

    a.elem("rect")
        .attr("width", size.x.to_pt())
        .attr("height", size.y.to_pt())
        .attr("fill", "transparent")
        .attr("stroke", "none");
}
```

Key points:
- Creates an `<a>` element (immediately, not lazy).
- Applies the current state's transform to the `<a>` (so the link is positioned/sized correctly).
- Three Destination variants:
  - Url: writes both `href` and `xlink:href` (for compatibility — href is SVG2, xlink:href is SVG1.1). The URL goes directly.
  - Position: TODO — same-page links not supported yet. Does nothing.
  - Location: needs the link_resolver (only present for svg_in_html and svg_in_bundle). Resolves the Location to a ResolvedLink via resolver.resolve(*loc), converts to a relative URI, and writes href/xlink:href. If no resolver or resolution fails, the `<a>` has no href (broken link).
- Inside the `<a>`, creates a transparent `<rect>` covering the link's size — this is the clickable area. fill="transparent" stroke="none" so it's invisible but receives clicks.

Important: both `href` and `xlink:href` are written for maximum compatibility with SVG renderers.

